<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Grunwald</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1410</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Tannenberg (1410), First Battle of Tannenberg, Battle of Žalgiris · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-teutonic-war">Polish–Lithuanian–Teutonic War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Grunwald, fought on 15 July 1410 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, was one of the largest battles of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. An allied army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/w-adys-aw-ii-jagie-o">Władysław II Jagiełło</a> and Vytautas crushed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Knights</a>, killing Grand Master <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulrich-von-jungingen">Ulrich von Jungingen</a> and much of the Order's leadership. The Order survived, but its military power never recovered.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-grunwald.jpg" alt="Battle of Grunwald" width="320" height="143" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan Matejko · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jan_Matejko,_Bitwa_pod_Grunwaldem.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
